<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Teozacoalco</h1><p class="st-meta">1000 CE – 1522 CE (approx.) · capital Teozacoalco</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Mixtec kingdom of the Mixteca Alta whose dynastic history is preserved in the Codex Zouche-Nuttall and the Map of Teozacoalco of 1580.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Teozacoalco, Chiyo Cahnu in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mixtecs">Mixtec</a>, was a royal seat in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mixteca-alta">Mixteca Alta</a> by about 1000. Its rulers were closely related by marriage to the lords of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/tilantongo">Tilantongo</a>, the senior Mixtec house, and its first dynasty appears in the codices of this period.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Like other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mixtecs">Mixtec</a> kingdoms, it was a small domain ruled by a hereditary lord and lady from a palace, drawing tribute from dependent villages. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/map-of-teozacoalco">Map of Teozacoalco</a>, painted for the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/relaciones-geograficas">Relaciones Geográficas</a>, lists its rulers in a long genealogy and helped scholars link the codices to real places and dates.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Teozacoalco fell under Aztec tribute in the late 15th century and came under Spanish rule after 1522, its native lords continuing as caciques under colonial authority.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1000 CE – 1522 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:79.60%;width:10.39%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1000 CE – 1522 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Teozacoalco</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Mixtec religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Mixtec</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Chiyo Cahnu</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1261&amp;focus=teozacoalco" aria-label="Teozacoalco on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2034 1546 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Teozacoalco lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M2354 1802L2321 1717"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M2321 1717h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2354 1802h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2354 1802h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1261&amp;focus=teozacoalco">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
